Of course freopen is shorter, I've just never used it in anger.

Nothing wrong with curiosity:

In the dim and distance past, when I was learning Vax C, I remembered doing an
experiment, "what if I close stdout", when that worked I tried adding a
"printf" statement to see what happened writing to a closed channel, finding
that also didn't crash I tried opening a new file on stdout.  My (unsurprising)
conclusion was that there was nothing "special" about stdout!

So my response to the post was based on the memory of something like:

	fclose (stdout);
	printf ("hello");
	stdout = fopen ("test", "w");
	printf ("again);

